<Base slug="algorithms/rest-period/" title="Rest period" description="Why a place you loved rests for a while before The Cousin suggests it again, and why clubs work the other way.">
  <header class="wrap phead">
    <p class="chapter">04 · The algorithms · Stage 3</p>
    <h1 class="h1" data-split="lines" data-intro>A place you loved should rest before it comes back.</h1>
    <div class="headrow" data-reveal="up" data-intro data-delay="0.3">
      <p class="lede muted">Without a rest, the place you loved last Saturday wins every Saturday. Good at first, boring by the third week.</p>
      <Status s="tested" />
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">In plain words</p>
    <div class="prose"><p>Every place you visit gets a small penalty that fades over time. The more you loved it, the sooner it returns. Places you disliked never come back. Clubs and communities are the opposite: going back is the point, so a club you liked gets a small bonus instead. And you can always ask for a place by name; that’s a pin, and a pin beats any rest.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">Watch it work</p>
    <Video v="V06" />
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">On the example</p>
    <div class="tbl" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>You said after</th><th>Rest</th><th>Comes back</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Loved it</td><td>Short</td><td>About a month</td></tr><tr><td>It was fine</td><td>Longer</td><td>About two months</td></tr><tr><td>Not for me</td><td>Forever</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>A club you liked</td><td>None: a bonus</td><td>Next time it meets</td></tr><tr><td>“Take me back to Kaveri”</td><td>Ignored: a pin</td><td>Tonight</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap row">
    <p class="chapter">For engineers</p>
    <details class="eng">
      <summary>The decay</summary>
      <div class="prose">
        <pre class="code">rest(x) = R · exp(−days_since / τ)      τ = 30 (loved), 60 (liked), ∞ (disliked)
club(x) = +B if liked, no decay</pre>
        <p>τ is the time it takes the penalty to fall to about a third. Both values are guesses tested in simulation; the models stage learns them per person.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</Base>
